      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bad4c757aa2c43f6bc506d8|full_name}: As ive come to notice, these moments already happen based on peoples ability to pay attention to certain parts or people in a conversation because of multiple factors. Sensory overload, EARMUFF mode, bad voice fall off, and our just someone talks lower across from you compared to the one on your side. Tbh, I feel this would help encourage proper group conversations instead of one another attempting to over talk the other because someone CAN be louder.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
